From dea13a14e7394be6060bbf490d2089bfd91499cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:37:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 092/108] gpu: shared memory shader reads through one R32_UINT
 texel buffer; pipeline IR dump

On Adreno/Turnip maxStorageBufferRange is 128 MB, so the 512 MB shared memory
was four storage buffers and every 32-bit vertex fetch word compiled to a
four-way switch (4 predicated isam + compares + nops). maxTexelBufferElements
is 2^27, so one R32_UINT uniform texel buffer view covers all of it: loads
become one texelFetch (binding 2 of the shared memory set). Writes
(memexport) keep the storage buffers. Cvar vulkan_shared_memory_texel_buffer
(default on, init-only; part of the precompile marker). Yusnaan view GPU
16.8 -> 16.0 ms per frame, Ark 15.8 -> 15.0 ms.

Diagnostics: vulkan_pipeline_ir_dump_ps=<PS hashes> with
vulkan_pipeline_statistics and monolithic pipelines logs the driver's
internal representations (NIR, IR3 assembly) of those pipelines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

